## gfx: Garlic's pixel layout for the native window
## (docs/design/garlic-browser.md, "Pixel layout").
##
## Lays a parsed document out in CSS pixels: the box model (margin, border,
## padding, width), block and inline flow with proportional text, lists,
## tables, simple flexbox and grid, images and form controls, then returns
## a display list in `draw.Op`s and the screen rectangle of every link.
## Written from CSS 2.1 chapters 8-10 and 16-17 (simplified: margins of
## adjoining blocks collapse, floats and positioning are ignored) and
## CSS Flexbox/Grid Level 1 (single-pass approximations).
##
## Text widths come from a table of Helvetica advance widths: the host has
## no measuring call yet, and each word is drawn at its own x so the small
## differences between fonts never add up along a line.

use html
use css
use draw
use page
use images

## The screen rectangle of a link, in page pixels.
pub struct Hit
    pub x float
    pub y float
    pub w float
    pub h float
    pub href str
    ## The form control's node for a click that uses it, else -1.
    pub node int
    ## The link's node (the `a` element) for a link's rectangle, else -1.
    pub anchor int

## The border box of a block-level element, for scripts that measure
## (`getBoundingClientRect`, `offsetWidth`): page coordinates.
pub struct Box
    pub node int
    pub x float
    pub y float
    pub w float
    pub h float
    ## How many drawing operations came before it: the shifts that move
    ## operations from an index on move the boxes recorded after it too.
    at int

## A laid-out page: its drawing operations, links and size.
pub struct Scene
    pub ops List[draw.Op]
    pub hits List[Hit]
    pub boxes List[Box]
    pub height float
    ## The canvas color (the `body` or `html` background, else white).
    pub bg int
    ## The text runs whose widths were estimated, not measured.
    pub probes List[Probe]
    ## Pictures drawn by the layout itself (inline SVG), by the `src` of their `Pic`.
    pub bits Map[str, images.Bitmap]

## A text run whose width the host can measure (docs/spec/std-app.md,
## std.app.13).
pub struct Probe
    pub text str
    pub size float
    pub bold bool
    pub italic bool
    ## The host font family: `sans`, `mono` or `serif`.
    pub font str

## The key of a run in the measured table.
pub fn probe_key(text str, size float, bold bool, italic bool, font str) str
    "{size}|{bold}|{italic}|{font}|{text}"

